{
 "slug": "iso-9001-2026-what-changed-from-2015",
 "title": "ISO 9001:2026: What Changed from 2015 and What It Means for You",
 "desc": "ISO 9001:2026 replaced the 2015 edition in September 2026. A clause-by-clause look at what changed, what did not, and who needs to act by September 2029.",
 "cats": [
  "iso"
 ],
 "tags": [
  "ISO 9001:2026",
  "quality management",
  "transition",
  "quality culture",
  "risk and opportunity"
 ],
 "body": "<p>ISO published the sixth edition of ISO 9001 on 16 September 2026. It replaces ISO 9001:2015, the edition that most certified organizations have worked to for a decade. If you hold a certificate, you have until 30 September 2029 to move to the new edition. If you are planning to get certified, you will soon be audited against it.</p>\n<p>The short version: this is an update, not a rebuild. Certification bodies describe the changes as evolutionary. The structure, the process approach, the plan-do-check-act cycle and risk-based thinking all stay. The new material is concentrated in leadership and planning.</p>\n<blockquote style=\"font-size:16.5px\">This article is based on ISO's announcement and on summaries published by certification bodies. It is not a substitute for the standard. Buy a copy of ISO 9001:2026 and confirm the requirements and your transition dates with your certification body.</blockquote>\n<h2>What changed, clause by clause</h2>\n<figure style=\"overflow-x:auto\"><svg role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Table-style diagram of ISO 9001 clauses 3 to 10 and Annex A, shaded by amount of change. Main changes are in clause 5 Leadership, clause 6 Planning and Annex A. Smaller changes are in clauses 3, 4, 7 and 10. Clauses 8 and 9 are largely unchanged.\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" viewBox=\"0 0 480.24 310.896\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\">\n <metadata>\n  <rdf:RDF xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xmlns:cc=\"http://creativecommons.org/ns#\" xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\">\n   <cc:Work>\n    <dc:type rdf:resource=\"http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/StillImage\"/>\n    <dc:date>2026-11-10T01:57:28.091284</dc:date>\n    <dc:format>image/svg+xml</dc:format>\n    <dc:creator>\n     <cc:Agent>\n      <dc:title>Matplotlib v3.11.2, https://matplotlib.org/</dc:title>\n     </cc:Agent>\n    </dc:creator>\n   </cc:Work>\n  </rdf:RDF>\n </metadata>\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 310.896 \nL 480.24 310.896 \nL 480.24 0 \nL 0 0 \nL 0 310.896 \nz\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 13.25952 54.258912 \nL 466.98048 54.258912 \nQ 470.73024 54.258912 470.73024 51.863904 \nL 470.73024 35.6976 \nQ 470.73024 33.302592 466.98048 33.302592 \nL 13.25952 33.302592 \nQ 9.50976 33.302592 9.50976 35.6976 \nL 9.50976 51.863904 \nQ 9.50976 54.258912 13.25952 54.258912 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p4b8ae579a2)\" style=\"fill: #cfe6f3; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_3\">\n    <path d=\"M 13.25952 80.005248 \nL 466.98048 80.005248 \nQ 470.73024 80.005248 470.73024 77.61024 \nL 470.73024 61.443936 \nQ 470.73024 59.048928 466.98048 59.048928 \nL 13.25952 59.048928 \nQ 9.50976 59.048928 9.50976 61.443936 \nL 9.50976 77.61024 \nQ 9.50976 80.005248 13.25952 80.005248 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p4b8ae579a2)\" style=\"fill: #cfe6f3; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_4\">\n    <path d=\"M 13.25952 105.751584 \nL 466.98048 105.751584 \nQ 470.73024 105.751584 470.73024 103.356576 \nL 470.73024 87.190272 \nQ 470.73024 84.795264 466.98048 84.795264 \nL 13.25952 84.795264 \nQ 9.50976 84.795264 9.50976 87.190272 \nL 9.50976 103.356576 \nQ 9.50976 105.751584 13.25952 105.751584 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p4b8ae579a2)\" style=\"fill: #fbe6d8; stroke: #e07a3a; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_5\">\n    <path d=\"M 13.25952 131.49792 \nL 466.98048 131.49792 \nQ 470.73024 131.49792 470.73024 129.102912 \nL 470.73024 112.936608 \nQ 470.73024 110.5416 466.98048 110.5416 \nL 13.25952 110.5416 \nQ 9.50976 110.5416 9.50976 112.936608 \nL 9.50976 129.102912 \nQ 9.50976 131.49792 13.25952 131.49792 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p4b8ae579a2)\" style=\"fill: #fbe6d8; stroke: #e07a3a; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_6\">\n    <path d=\"M 13.25952 157.244256 \nL 466.98048 157.244256 \nQ 470.73024 157.244256 470.73024 154.849248 \nL 470.73024 138.682944 \nQ 470.73024 136.287936 466.98048 136.287936 \nL 13.25952 136.287936 \nQ 9.50976 136.287936 9.50976 138.682944 \nL 9.50976 154.849248 \nQ 9.50976 157.244256 13.25952 157.244256 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p4b8ae579a2)\" style=\"fill: #cfe6f3; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_7\">\n    <path d=\"M 13.25952 182.990592 \nL 466.98048 182.990592 \nQ 470.73024 182.990592 470.73024 180.595584 \nL 470.73024 164.42928 \nQ 470.73024 162.034272 466.98048 162.034272 \nL 13.25952 162.034272 \nQ 9.50976 162.034272 9.50976 164.42928 \nL 9.50976 180.595584 \nQ 9.50976 182.990592 13.25952 182.990592 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p4b8ae579a2)\" style=\"fill: #eef3f9; stroke: #9ab0c8; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_8\">\n    <path d=\"M 13.25952 208.736928 \nL 466.98048 208.736928 \nQ 470.73024 208.736928 470.73024 206.34192 \nL 470.73024 190.175616 \nQ 470.73024 187.780608 466.98048 187.780608 \nL 13.25952 187.780608 \nQ 9.50976 187.780608 9.50976 190.175616 \nL 9.50976 206.34192 \nQ 9.50976 208.736928 13.25952 208.736928 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p4b8ae579a2)\" style=\"fill: #eef3f9; stroke: #9ab0c8; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_9\">\n    <path d=\"M 13.25952 234.483264 \nL 466.98048 234.483264 \nQ 470.73024 234.483264 470.73024 232.088256 \nL 470.73024 215.921952 \nQ 470.73024 213.526944 466.98048 213.526944 \nL 13.25952 213.526944 \nQ 9.50976 213.526944 9.50976 215.921952 \nL 9.50976 232.088256 \nQ 9.50976 234.483264 13.25952 234.483264 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p4b8ae579a2)\" style=\"fill: #cfe6f3; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_10\">\n    <path d=\"M 13.25952 260.2296 \nL 466.98048 260.2296 \nQ 470.73024 260.2296 470.73024 257.834592 \nL 470.73024 241.668288 \nQ 470.73024 239.27328 466.98048 239.27328 \nL 13.25952 239.27328 \nQ 9.50976 239.27328 9.50976 241.668288 \nL 9.50976 257.834592 \nQ 9.50976 260.2296 13.25952 260.2296 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p4b8ae579a2)\" style=\"fill: #fbe6d8; stroke: #e07a3a; stroke-width: 1.1; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_11\">\n    <path d=\"M 74.19312 296.15472 \nL 84.50496 296.15472 \nQ 88.25472 296.15472 88.25472 293.759712 \nL 88.25472 285.377184 \nQ 88.25472 282.982176 84.50496 282.982176 \nL 74.19312 282.982176 \nQ 70.44336 282.982176 70.44336 285.377184 \nL 70.44336 293.759712 \nQ 70.44336 296.15472 74.19312 296.15472 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p4b8ae579a2)\" style=\"fill: #fbe6d8; stroke: #e07a3a; stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_12\">\n    <path d=\"M 200.74752 296.15472 \nL 211.05936 296.15472 \nQ 214.80912 296.15472 214.80912 293.759712 \nL 214.80912 285.377184 \nQ 214.80912 282.982176 211.05936 282.982176 \nL 200.74752 282.982176 \nQ 196.99776 282.982176 196.99776 285.377184 \nL 196.99776 293.759712 \nQ 196.99776 296.15472 200.74752 296.15472 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p4b8ae579a2)\" style=\"fill: #cfe6f3; stroke: #0b6fa4; stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_13\">\n    <path d=\"M 327.30192 296.15472 \nL 337.61376 296.15472 \nQ 341.36352 296.15472 341.36352 293.759712 \nL 341.36352 285.377184 \nQ 341.36352 282.982176 337.61376 282.982176 \nL 327.30192 282.982176 \nQ 323.55216 282.982176 323.55216 285.377184 \nL 323.55216 293.759712 \nQ 323.55216 296.15472 327.30192 296.15472 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p4b8ae579a2)\" style=\"fill: #eef3f9; stroke: #9ab0c8; stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_1\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 11.5px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"29.196\" y=\"47.964102\" transform=\"rotate(-0 29.196 47.964102)\">3</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_2\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"52.632\" y=\"47.054678\" transform=\"rotate(-0 52.632 47.054678)\">Terms and definitions</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_3\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.4px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #4a5568\" x=\"183.8736\" y=\"46.836416\" transform=\"rotate(-0 183.8736 46.836416)\">The harmonized terms are now listed in the standard itself</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_4\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 11.5px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"29.196\" y=\"73.710438\" transform=\"rotate(-0 29.196 73.710438)\">4</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_5\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"52.632\" y=\"72.801014\" transform=\"rotate(-0 52.632 72.801014)\">Context of the organization</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_6\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.4px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #4a5568\" x=\"183.8736\" y=\"72.582752\" transform=\"rotate(-0 183.8736 72.582752)\">Climate change wording from the 2024 amendment is built in</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_7\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 11.5px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"29.196\" y=\"99.456774\" transform=\"rotate(-0 29.196 99.456774)\">5</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_8\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"52.632\" y=\"98.54735\" transform=\"rotate(-0 52.632 98.54735)\">Leadership</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_9\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.4px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #4a5568\" x=\"183.8736\" y=\"98.329088\" transform=\"rotate(-0 183.8736 98.329088)\">Quality culture and ethical behaviour; policy tied to strategy</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_10\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 11.5px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"29.196\" y=\"125.20311\" transform=\"rotate(-0 29.196 125.20311)\">6</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_11\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"52.632\" y=\"124.293686\" transform=\"rotate(-0 52.632 124.293686)\">Planning</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_12\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.4px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #4a5568\" x=\"183.8736\" y=\"124.075424\" transform=\"rotate(-0 183.8736 124.075424)\">Risks and opportunities split; planning of changes reinforced</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_13\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 11.5px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"29.196\" y=\"150.949446\" transform=\"rotate(-0 29.196 150.949446)\">7</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_14\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"52.632\" y=\"150.040022\" transform=\"rotate(-0 52.632 150.040022)\">Support</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_15\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.4px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #4a5568\" x=\"183.8736\" y=\"149.82176\" transform=\"rotate(-0 183.8736 149.82176)\">Awareness now covers quality culture and ethical behaviour</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_16\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 11.5px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"29.196\" y=\"176.695782\" transform=\"rotate(-0 29.196 176.695782)\">8</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_17\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"52.632\" y=\"175.786358\" transform=\"rotate(-0 52.632 175.786358)\">Operation</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_18\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.4px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #4a5568\" x=\"183.8736\" y=\"175.568096\" transform=\"rotate(-0 183.8736 175.568096)\">Wording and layout only</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_19\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 11.5px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"29.196\" y=\"202.442118\" transform=\"rotate(-0 29.196 202.442118)\">9</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_20\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"52.632\" y=\"201.532694\" transform=\"rotate(-0 52.632 201.532694)\">Performance evaluation</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_21\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.4px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #4a5568\" x=\"183.8736\" y=\"201.314432\" transform=\"rotate(-0 183.8736 201.314432)\">Minimal change</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_22\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 11.5px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"29.196\" y=\"228.188454\" transform=\"rotate(-0 29.196 228.188454)\">10</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_23\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"52.632\" y=\"227.27903\" transform=\"rotate(-0 52.632 227.27903)\">Improvement</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_24\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.4px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #4a5568\" x=\"183.8736\" y=\"227.060768\" transform=\"rotate(-0 183.8736 227.060768)\">Continual improvement requirements consolidated</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_25\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 11.5px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"29.196\" y=\"253.93479\" transform=\"rotate(-0 29.196 253.93479)\">A</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_26\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"52.632\" y=\"253.025366\" transform=\"rotate(-0 52.632 253.025366)\">Annex A (guidance)</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_27\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.4px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #4a5568\" x=\"183.8736\" y=\"252.807104\" transform=\"rotate(-0 183.8736 252.807104)\">Rewritten and expanded, clause by clause; adds no requirements</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_28\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 9px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"97.62912\" y=\"292.842374\" transform=\"rotate(-0 97.62912 292.842374)\">Main changes</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_29\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 9px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"224.18352\" y=\"292.842374\" transform=\"rotate(-0 224.18352 292.842374)\">Smaller changes</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_30\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 9px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"350.73792\" y=\"292.842374\" transform=\"rotate(-0 350.73792 292.842374)\">Largely unchanged</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_31\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 10.5px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: middle; fill: #0b2a5a\" x=\"240.12\" y=\"20.05774\" transform=\"rotate(-0 240.12 20.05774)\">ISO 9001:2026 compared with ISO 9001:2015, by clause</text>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"p4b8ae579a2\">\n   <rect x=\"5.76\" y=\"5.76\" width=\"468.72\" height=\"299.376\"/>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Where ISO 9001:2026 differs from ISO 9001:2015. Compiled from summaries by DNV, DQS and SGS.</figcaption></figure>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Clause</th><th>What changed</th><th>What to check in your system</th></tr>\n<tr><td>3 Terms</td><td>The terms shared by all ISO management system standards are now listed in the standard, with less reliance on ISO 9000.</td><td>Nothing to change. Use the new definitions when you train auditors.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4.1, 4.2 Context</td><td>The climate change wording added by the 2024 amendment is now part of the text.</td><td>Your context review should record whether climate change is a relevant issue, and why or why not.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>5.1.1 Leadership</td><td>Top management must promote quality culture and ethical behaviour.</td><td>How do leaders show this in practice? An auditor will ask them directly.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>5.2 Quality policy</td><td>The policy must reflect the organization's context and support its strategic direction more explicitly.</td><td>Read the policy next to your strategy. Does one follow from the other?</td></tr>\n<tr><td>6.1 Risks and opportunities</td><td>Split into subclauses 6.1.1 to 6.1.3, with actions for risks and actions for opportunities addressed separately.</td><td>If your register lists only threats, add opportunities and the actions tied to each.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>6.3 Planning of changes</td><td>Requirements reinforced, with more emphasis on communicating, monitoring and reviewing changes.</td><td>Pick two recent changes and trace how they were planned and followed up.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>7.1.4, 7.3 Support</td><td>The work environment and awareness clauses now refer to quality culture and ethical behaviour.</td><td>Update induction and refresher training, and keep a record that people received it.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>8 Operation, 9 Performance evaluation</td><td>Minimal change: wording and layout.</td><td>Renumber references if clause numbers moved.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>10 Improvement</td><td>Continual improvement requirements consolidated.</td><td>Renumber references.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Annex A</td><td>Rewritten and expanded to explain the intent of clauses 4 to 10. It is guidance and adds no requirements.</td><td>Read it. It is the best free explanation of what auditors will look for.</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h2>The two changes that need real work</h2>\n<h3>Quality culture and ethical behaviour</h3>\n<p>These are now explicit requirements on top management, and people across the organization must be aware of them. This is the change most likely to produce audit findings, because it cannot be met with a document alone. An auditor will look for evidence in behaviour: what happens when someone reports a problem, how a missed shipment date is weighed against releasing product that is not right, and what leaders talk about when they walk the floor.</p>\n<p>Practical evidence includes a short statement of expected conduct that people recognize, leaders who can describe how they reinforce it, a way to raise concerns without penalty, and examples of decisions where quality or honesty came before convenience.</p>\n<h3>Risks and opportunities, separately</h3>\n<p>The 2015 edition asked for \"risks and opportunities\" in one breath, and many organizations responded with a risk register and nothing else. The new edition separates the two. You will need to show that you look for opportunities, such as a new market, a better process or a new technology, and that you plan actions for them as deliberately as for threats. Our article on <a href=\"post/iso-9001-risk-based-thinking-in-practice.html\">risk-based thinking in practice</a> gives a worked example.</p>\n<h2>What did not change</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The ten-clause structure shared with ISO 14001 and ISO 45001.</li>\n<li>The process approach and the plan-do-check-act cycle.</li>\n<li>Clause 8, where most of your operating procedures sit.</li>\n<li>The standard remains technology-neutral. It adds no specific requirement about artificial intelligence or digital tools.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Who needs to do what</h2>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Your situation</th><th>What to do</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Certified to ISO 9001:2015</td><td>Plan your transition for a scheduled surveillance or recertification audit before 30 September 2029. Do not leave it to the final year.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Working toward first certification</td><td>Build to the 2026 edition now. Certification bodies report that new certificates to the 2015 edition stop being issued in spring 2028, and a certificate issued to the old edition would expire with the transition period.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Not certified, but customers ask for conformance</td><td>Use the 2026 edition as your reference and tell customers which edition your system follows.</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>The transition rules are set by the international accreditation community, now called Global ACI, and applied by your certification body. Our <a href=\"post/iso-9001-2026-transition-plan.html\">step-by-step transition plan</a> sets out the work in order.</p>\n<h2>Key points</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>ISO 9001:2026 was published on 16 September 2026. ISO 9001:2015 certificates stop being valid after 30 September 2029.</li>\n<li>Most of your system stays as it is. The work is in leadership (culture, ethics, policy) and planning (risks, opportunities, changes).</li>\n<li>Culture and ethics need evidence in behaviour, so start with your leadership team.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Want a second pair of eyes?</strong> Chmltech helps Canadian organizations build, simplify and audit quality management systems. <a href=\"../book.html\">Book a strategy call</a> or <a href=\"../contact.html\">ask a question</a>.</p>\n<h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.iso.org/quality-management/iso-9001-2026\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">ISO: ISO 9001:2026, what businesses need to know</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.dnv.us/assurance/Management-Systems/new-iso/transition/iso-9001-revision/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">DNV: ISO 9001:2026 standard revision</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.dqsglobal.com/en/explore/blog/iso-9001-2026-changes-timeline-transition\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">DQS: ISO 9001:2026, key changes, timeline and transition checklist</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.dqsglobal.com/en/explore/blog/iso-9001-2026-transition\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">DQS: ISO 9001:2026 is here (transition)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.sgs.com/en-gb/showcases/iso-9001-2026-key-updates-and-transition-guidance\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">SGS: ISO 9001:2026 key updates and transition guidance</a></li></ul>\n<h2>More in this series</h2><ul><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-2026-transition-plan.html\">Your ISO 9001:2026 transition plan</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-for-small-and-mid-sized-businesses.html\">ISO 9001 for small and mid-sized businesses</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-internal-audits-that-find-real-problems.html\">Internal audits that find real problems</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-risk-based-thinking-in-practice.html\">Risk-based thinking in practice</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-and-ai-using-ai-tools-inside-a-quality-system.html\">ISO 9001 and AI</a></li><li><a href=\"post/integrated-management-system-iso-9001-14001-45001.html\">Integrating ISO 9001, ISO 14001 and ISO 45001</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-management-review-that-leadership-finds-useful.html\">Management review that leadership finds useful</a></li></ul>",
